[{"code":"top_level_record_changed","severity":"error","span":{"file":"Main.beni","start":{"line":56,"col":42},"end":{"line":56,"col":49}},"title":"TOP-LEVEL RECORD CHANGED","message":"`Main.bump` changes `ps[*]#Pt.0` in place, but it is `origin`, a top-level\nvalue.\n\n56|                    { model | n = total (bump ps) }\n                                            ^^^^^^^ the record is changed in place here\n\n21|origin = Pt { x = 0 }\n   ^^^^^^ the top-level record is defined here\n\nA top-level value is shared by every part of the program and never changes:\nchanged in place, it would change for every part that reads it.\n\nMake `origin` a function that builds a fresh record at each call, `origin ⊤`, or\nchange a copy: `{ Record.copy origin | … }`.\n\nThis is the language's rule for top-level values, whether or not anything else\nreads the record (ownership-checker.md §31.4)."}]
